						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Grin, I did retail.. at CompUSA was not too bad.. I actually liked it, I also run a pet store with my wife... I feel your pain though.. so many times morons get hired to manage a place and they do not know squat, just because they got a damn BA in English they think they will make a great manager.  <br />
<br />
The thing to realize is that it is just your job to serve people, even if they are stupid, as alot of people are very demanding, to the guy who says &quot;hello mate&quot; that is not bad.. just say hello back, its a big acting job, hey I listen to people talk about their pets and act like I give a crap, when in reality I am thinking ok enough of your pet.. you can leave now, but I do not show that. I keep on smiling and saying aww how nice.. oh really.. wow.. your pet is special.. <br />
<br />
retail never really pays much, we pay our employees 8 bucks Canadian.. which in reality is like 6 bucks American, Canadians seem to think they have a better way of life, but me being an American living in Canada for 3 years think they are on serious crack, Canada is a over taxed country, and their cost of goods is rediculous.. Free health  my butt, 15% tax rate is rediculous and Toronto is no cleaner than San Francisco.<br />
<br />
anyway sorry to hear about how bad your day was.. the best way to fix your situation is to get up off the tac thats in your behind, see only when the tac in your butt hurts enough do you get up and do something about it.. <br />
<br />
I would work at a retail store again, but would prefer to work at night doing stock where I do not have to interact with peeps, but I am moving to a small town called Mt. Airy in North Carolina, and let me just say that since it is a small town working retail will be much easier.. heck the home depot parking lot is not even half full, when I worked at hOme depot in California the parking lot was half full at 6am when the contractors came in.. was full by 11am and stayed that way till we closed.. working retail in a city always sucks becaues there are way to many customers for how many workers are working because the managers are trying to save a buck.. and granted sometimes they are not making enough to pay for more workers.  I know that for a fact, then there are peeps who think the store manager owes them something so they steal, or do not do their work.. so some other hard working person will pick up the slack of that person also.. and so the hard working person gets burned out and thus the downward spiral.. <br />
<br />
I get a kick out of helping hard cases.. I feel that when I help a hard case that someone else could not, I become more of a asset and makes me feel good that I overcame a jerk of a customer.  Most of the time people just want someone to listen to what they have to say.						</td>
